& [DataDesignModel] is stable
  + [conceptual_model] is one future physical observation represented by a receipt without making the receipt its own proof
  + [logical_identity] is receipt_profile plus scanner_profile plus candidate_root plus root_identity plus root_volume_guid_path plus predecessor content bindings
  + [physical_model] is strict serde JSON and pure Rust value validation
  + [natural_identity] is the complete serialized receipt content
  + [technical_identity] is a canonical SHA-256 of that serialized content in later consumers
  + [source_data] is future scanner-owned physical observation
  + [derived_projection] is TopologyReceipt
  + [freshness_rule] is the existing issue-to-expiry interval plus future path and inventory revalidation
  + [recompute_rule] is rescan rather than edit a receipt
  + [lineage_rule] is source observation to receipt to receipt digest to consumption evidence
  - never: patch a receipt to repair stale or missing source observation

& [DataDesignQualityGate] is passed
  + [identity_check] is four profile/authority identities and three root evidence identities are explicit
  + [layer_separation_check] is conceptual observation, logical receipt, and physical JSON remain distinct
  + [hierarchy_check] is nested StrongFileIdentity distinguished from candidate and final-path references
  + [transform_check] is future observation-to-receipt and current JSON-to-validated-form contracts are explicit
  + [constraint_check] is requiredness, strict fields, uniqueness of profiles, grammar, bounds, and freshness are explicit
  + [projection_check] is receipt identified as derived evidence with rescan invalidation
  + [provenance_check] is source, profile, policy, inventory, and admission bindings preserved
  + [model_selection_check] is pure structured form selected without adding persistence technology
  + [implementation_check] is one existing module boundary follows the stable form and transform boundary
  + [anti_pattern_check] is no database-first, object-first, UI-state-first, or schema-theater drift

